@if(!$compact)<details class="od-department-method od-panel"><summary>Scoring rules, evidence coverage & limitations</summary><p>On-time action completion (35%): actions due in the reporting window completed by their deadline ÷ actions due, including still-overdue actions. Missing completion dates earn no credit; more than 20% missing makes this measure unavailable. Still-open actions due today are not treated as late.</p><p>Overdue action control (25%): 100 × max(0, 1 − weighted overdue exposure ÷ total eligible action weight). Low / Moderate / High priority weights are 1 / 2 / 3. Overdue exposure multiplies that weight by 1 + min(3, days overdue ÷ 30). Completed actions due within the window and open actions due through today form the denominator. Open future actions earn no points. Older overdue actions remain included.</p><p>Scheduled audits completed (20%) and recorded objectives achieved (20%): completed/achieved records ÷ obligations due in the reporting window. These reflect recorded status, not independent verification. Scores average available measures using their model weights; missing measures limit coverage and do not earn a perfect score.</p><p>Ranking is within identical metric/source-workflow coverage groups, not a company-wide league table. A minimum of {{ $performance['minimum_records'] }} eligible records, {{ $performance['minimum_coverage'] }}% metric coverage and 80% date/status completeness applies. This is a starting operational model; it is not a performance appraisal or an ESG rating. Reporting incidents or creating records does not earn or lose points.</p><p>Training completion and review turnaround are not scored until reliable department attribution, required training plans and timing targets are connected. No historical change is invented from today's mutable records.</p><p>{{ $performance['unassigned'] }} non-cancelled source records could not be linked to an active department by exact ID; they are excluded from departmental comparisons.</p><div class="od-department-source-list">@foreach($performance['sources'] as $source)<span>{{ ['mitigations'=>'Risk mitigation actions','corrective'=>'Corrective actions','issues'=>'Audit findings','hseissues'=>'HSE actions','nearmiss'=>'Near-miss actions','audit'=>'Scheduled audits','objectives'=>'Department objectives'][$source['name']] ?? $source['name'] }}: <strong>{{ $source['available'] ? 'Available' : 'Missing department, status or deadline fields' }}</strong></span>@endforeach</div></details>@endif
